Key Takeaway

Azure Load Balancer is a Layer 4 networking service that distributes TCP and UDP traffic across multiple Azure resources to improve availability, scalability, and fault tolerance. By using frontend IP configurations, backend pools, health probes, and load balancing rules, Azure Administrators can ensure applications remain responsive and available even during infrastructure failures. Understanding when to use Azure Load Balancer versus Application Gateway, Traffic Manager, or Front Door is an important skill for the AZ-104 exam and real-world Azure administration.
